<header class="wrap hero">
  <div class="eyebrow">🧽 GitHub continuity · ChatGPT replay continuity · live web continuity</div>
  <h1>Jay's World Map is the front door.</h1>
  <p class="lead">This live homepage binds the repository map, the replay conversation, and the public web page into one continuity surface. The page presents the map; the receipts carry authority; replay proves the state.</p>
  <div class="actions">
    <a class="btn" href="WORLD_MAP.md">Replay WORLD_MAP.md</a>
    <a class="btn secondary" href="CONTINUITY_INDEX.json">Open Continuity Index</a>
    <a class="btn green" href="ACTIVE_LANES.json">Open Active Lanes</a>
  </div>
  <div class="banner mono"><strong>Continuity target:</strong> GitHub ↔ ChatGPT ↔ Live Web Page. No fake green. No hidden homepage owner. Jay's World Map stays visible.</div>
</header>
<main>
  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="section-head"><div><h2>Operating order</h2><p class="note">The repo is organized so new work starts from the map instead of from memory.</p></div></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card flat"><span class="kicker">Layer 0</span><h3>Family root</h3><p>Family remains the root layer. Project narratives do not outrank family.</p></article>
      <article class="card flat"><span class="kicker">Layer 1</span><h3>Trust foundation</h3><p>ALMS, proof rules, receipt discipline, and source assets.</p></article>
      <article class="card flat"><span class="kicker">Layer 2</span><h3>Consumers</h3><p>Goblin Court, Meme Court, Clown Court, and ZTVS Replay Map.</p></article>
      <article class="card flat"><span class="kicker">Layer 3</span><h3>Public surfaces</h3><p>Pages, receipts, replay maps, Zora artifacts, and identity anchors.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="grid two">
      <article class="card">
        <h2>Replay rules</h2>
        <div class="rule"><div class="num">1</div><div><b>Receipts over narrative.</b><p>Narrative explains; it does not override the record.</p></div></div>
        <div class="rule"><div class="num">2</div><div><b>No fake green.</b><p>No status is promoted without a receipt-backed path.</p></div></div>
        <div class="rule"><div class="num">3</div><div><b>UI is not authority.</b><p>Dashboards and pages are presentation layers. Replay proves.</p></div></div>
      </article>
      <aside class="card">
        <h2>Current state</h2>
        <div class="status-grid">
          <div class="status"><strong>Continuity</strong><span>GREEN_ON_MASTER</span></div>
          <div class="status"><strong>Active Lanes</strong><span>NO GREEN CLAIMS</span></div>
          <div class="status"><strong>Homepage</strong><span>World Map</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="mono" style="margin-top:16px;color:var(--muted)">Source path: WORLD_MAP.md → CONTINUITY_INDEX.json → ACTIVE_LANES.json → live index.html</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section" id="anchor-001">
    <div class="section-head"><div><h2>Anchor 001</h2><p class="note">Classified by WORLD_MAP.md commit 2117ead9e0dcf8e4697f3bcef648b6021547e794.</p></div></div>
    <article class="card">
      <span class="kicker">Public replayable identity root</span>
      <h3>jsonwisdom/Welcome-to-JSONWISDOM</h3>
      <p>Anchor 001 is the public identity root and orientation doorway for Jason Wisdom / Jay Wisdom / JSONWisdom. It is narrator and orientation layer only; it does not promote claims into proof.</p>
      <div class="banner mono"><strong>Boundary:</strong> Identity may be public and replayable without becoming sacred. No downstream lane goes GREEN without receipts.</div>
    </article>
  </section>
